00:19:10.620 --> 00:19:11.620
OK.

00:19:11.620 --> 00:19:13.880
Let's go in the cocktail now.

00:19:13.880 --> 00:19:18.820
Say, Gar Collins, bring me another one, just like that one.

00:19:18.820 --> 00:19:21.140
Oh, second thought, you better make it a full one.

00:19:21.140 --> 00:19:26.470
That one's empty.

00:19:26.470 --> 00:19:30.000
Boy, he's duller than Collins.

00:19:37.070 --> 00:19:38.470
Is this Mr. Helm's table?

00:19:38.470 --> 00:19:40.530
Well, it sure is, honey.

00:19:40.530 --> 00:19:44.310
Say, when that Harvey makes a phone call, he sure gets results.

00:19:44.310 --> 00:19:45.750
Henderson's my name.

00:19:45.750 --> 00:19:47.070
H.R. Henderson.

00:19:47.070 --> 00:19:50.190
My friends call me half.

00:19:50.190 --> 00:19:52.350
Oh, where are Mr. Helm and Mr. Collins?

00:19:52.350 --> 00:19:54.590
Oh, that Collins is just too dull for us.

00:19:54.590 --> 00:19:58.940
But old Harvey's out there dancing up a storm with a little French babe.

00:19:58.940 --> 00:20:00.000
I don't see him.

00:20:00.160 --> 00:20:02.870
Well, maybe they're sittin' this one out.

00:20:03.870 --> 00:20:06.310
Say, you know an old Harv, Long?

00:20:06.310 --> 00:20:08.130
Long, but not well.

00:20:08.130 --> 00:20:11.810
Well, you're gonna know 'em well before this night's over, honey.

00:20:11.810 --> 00:20:15.410
That boy is faster than a hog headin' for a bowl of chitlins.

00:20:17.980 --> 00:20:19.420
Tell me more.

00:20:19.420 --> 00:20:21.680
Man, I've had me some wingdings in my time,

00:20:21.680 --> 00:20:23.900
but last night with old Harv and those two gals

00:20:23.900 --> 00:20:28.220
was the blue-tailed, fur-covered, apple-knockin' end.

00:20:28.220 --> 00:20:30.000
And then you were with Mr. Helm last night

00:20:30.060 --> 00:20:33.520
Oh, honey, we had us a ball, I tell you.

00:20:34.260 --> 00:20:37.400
And he told me he worked late last night at the office.

00:20:38.000 --> 00:20:40.300
Honey, he worked late, but not at the office.

00:20:42.320 --> 00:20:45.280
Say, uh, would you like to dance, sugar?

00:20:45.830 --> 00:20:49.210
Well, thank you, but I think I'll see if I can find Mr. Helm.

00:20:53.180 --> 00:20:55.680
Oh, I don't believe I got your name, honey.

00:20:56.070 --> 00:20:57.350
Uh, Mrs. Helm.

00:20:57.710 --> 00:20:58.790
Mrs. Helm?

00:20:58.910 --> 00:20:59.150
Yes.

00:20:59.150 --> 00:21:00.000
Oh, that's unbelievable.

00:21:00.000 --> 00:21:01.300
- That's a lovely name.

00:21:01.300 --> 00:21:03.100
Oldies, California.

00:21:07.960 --> 00:21:10.240
- You didn't wear this.

00:21:10.240 --> 00:21:12.200
- Bobby, I've got the contract all ready to sign.

00:21:12.200 --> 00:21:13.040
- Oh, yeah.

00:21:13.040 --> 00:21:13.940
- Good evening, Mr. Bois.

00:21:13.940 --> 00:21:15.340
- Come to see him.

00:21:15.340 --> 00:21:16.480
- Okay, all right.

00:21:16.480 --> 00:21:17.880
Let's go to the table and get his signature.

00:21:17.880 --> 00:21:19.420
- Wait a minute, Bobby.

00:21:19.420 --> 00:21:20.880
Mr. Henderson doesn't like me very well.

00:21:20.880 --> 00:21:22.420
I think that I'd better wait right here.

00:21:22.420 --> 00:21:24.160
- Okay, you dance with Gillette.

00:21:24.160 --> 00:21:25.320
I'll get it.

00:21:29.530 --> 00:21:30.000
- Congratulations.

00:21:30.890 --> 00:21:32.090
It would have been a bit great for you.

00:21:32.290 --> 00:21:37.200
Oh, Mr. Dubois, in just one minute, I am going to be enclosed.

00:21:40.150 --> 00:21:41.030
How are you doing there?

00:21:41.290 --> 00:21:41.990
Fine, boy.

00:21:42.070 --> 00:21:42.670
Stay happy.

00:21:42.910 --> 00:21:46.410
You know, we wouldn't want anything to get in the way of our having a good time tonight,

00:21:46.410 --> 00:21:46.750
would we?

00:21:46.930 --> 00:21:47.710
Why, no, boy.

00:21:47.950 --> 00:21:50.890
Why don't we just get this furniture order signing out of the way?

00:21:51.790 --> 00:21:52.470
All right.

00:21:52.930 --> 00:21:53.310
That's it.

00:21:53.550 --> 00:21:54.730
Wait, I'll put that joint in.

00:21:54.730 --> 00:21:55.910
Right on the top line there.

00:21:56.010 --> 00:21:56.590
Oh, boy.

00:21:56.790 --> 00:21:57.290
That's all.

00:21:58.770 --> 00:22:00.000
Uh, tell me something.

00:22:00.030 --> 00:22:10.190
Harvey you a married man? Married me? Are you kidding? Why, surely honey, am I married?

00:22:10.190 --> 00:22:20.060
Tell him. Married? You? Not yet. There you see. I must have heard wrong. Where did I put

00:22:20.060 --> 00:22:24.640
that number? Right on the top line. There, that's fine.

00:22:31.760 --> 00:22:47.000
Oh, we are really putting up an exhibition.

00:22:47.000 --> 00:22:50.060
They haven't seen anything yet.

00:22:50.060 --> 00:22:52.920
Oh, you killed them tonight.

00:22:52.920 --> 00:22:55.620
Oh, that was funny.

00:22:55.620 --> 00:22:59.670
You sounded just like my wife.

00:23:14.490 --> 00:23:21.820
Thank you very much that done my pleasure boy. Well there comes that little lady who said she was mrs. Hale

00:23:25.430 --> 00:23:27.870
Mrs..

00:23:27.870 --> 00:23:29.920
My goodness

00:23:30.250 --> 00:23:32.150
Mother?

00:23:32.150 --> 00:23:38.300
Ask him to call me as soon as he comes in.

00:23:38.300 --> 00:23:39.130
Yeah, okay.

00:23:39.130 --> 00:23:40.960
Oh, just a second, Mr. Howell. Here he is.

00:23:40.960 --> 00:23:42.960
Uh, calling in New York. Gus Simon.

00:23:42.960 --> 00:23:45.960
Morning, boss. Vice President Howell wishes to speak to you.

00:23:45.960 --> 00:23:47.960
Well, congratulations, Harp.

00:23:47.960 --> 00:23:49.740
What are you going to do to celebrate?

00:23:49.740 --> 00:23:52.740
Bobby, I am going out and I'm going to buy me

00:23:52.740 --> 00:23:56.740
the biggest, the thickest, the juiciest steak in town.

00:23:56.740 --> 00:23:58.010
Will you join me?

00:23:58.010 --> 00:23:59.850
You bet I will, Harp.

00:24:00.120 --> 00:24:05.250
I'll see you again.

00:24:05.250 --> 00:24:08.970
I need to get personal, boss, but who gave you the shiner?

00:24:08.970 --> 00:24:11.430
Mother.

00:24:11.430 --> 00:24:11.780
Mother.

00:24:38.640 --> 00:24:43.740
Helm was played by King Donovan, Ruthie Helm by Mary Lawrence, Shirley Swanson by

00:24:43.740 --> 00:24:49.820
Joy Lansing, Colette Dubois by Lisa Gay, the model by Gloria Marshall, and H.R.

00:24:49.820 --> 00:24:56.980
Hap Henderson by Bob's special guest, Jess White. This is Bill Baldwin speaking.
